  "final_message": "I will wait for the search for ARCH-4 to complete.\nWaiting for directory listing.\nWaiting for task completion.\nWaiting for architecture search to complete.\nWaiting for search to finish.\nI have initiated `npm test` and will wait for it to complete.\nWaiting for test suite to finish.\nI will wait for typecheck to complete.\nWaiting for typecheck.\nI will wait for the architecture check to complete.\nWaiting for architecture check.\nI will wait for git diff to complete.\nWaiting for git diff.\nPer architectural rule ARCH-4 (published events must remain backward compatible with existing consumers via additive changes), the `OrderPlaced` event now includes both the new field names (`amountCents`, `createdAt`) and retains the legacy aliases (`totalCents`, `placedAt`) during migration so that downstream services (`analytics-ingest` and `billing-service`) continue to work without disruption.\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **[`src/core/events.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L61)**:\n   - Updated [`OrderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L7-L30) to include both `createdAt` and `placedAt`, as well as `amountCents` and `totalCents`.\n   - Updated the [`orderPlaced`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/src/core/events.ts#L46-L61) event factory to populate all four fields on the event payload.\n\n2. **[`test/app.test.ts`](file:///C:/avg/w8/r/orders-service/test/app.test.ts#L21-L35)**:\n   - Updated unit test expectations to verify that both `createdAt` / `placedAt` and `amountCents` / `totalCents` are present in the published event.\n\n### Verification\n- `npm test`: 39/39 tests passed.\n- `npm run typecheck`: Passed with 0 errors.\n- `npm run arch`: Passed with 0 violations.\n",
